      "text": "1. **Calculate the base of the triangle:** The base of the triangle is the horizontal distance between the vertices $(0,0)$ and $(7,12)$. This distance can be calculated using the distance formula between two points:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Base} = \\sqrt{(7-0)^2 + (12-0)^2} = \\sqrt{7^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{49 + 144} = \\sqrt{193}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the height of the triangle:** The height of the triangle is the vertical distance from the base of the triangle to the vertex $(7,12)$.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Height} = 12 - 0 = 12\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of the triangle:** The formula for the area of a triangle is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{Base} \\times \\text{Height}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the values we found:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\sqrt{193} \\times 12\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the expression:** Simplify the expression inside the area formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 \\times \\sqrt{193} = 6 \\times \\sqrt{193}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Approximate the value:** Calculate the numerical value of the area:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times \\sqrt{193} \\approx 6 \\times 13.898 = 83.388\n   \\]\n\n6. **Round to the nearest tenth:** Round the final answer to the nearest tenth:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} \\approx 83.4\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is \\boxed{83.4} square units.",
